---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  locale="en"
  slug="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy — KickoffWhen"
  description="KickoffWhen does not collect any personally identifiable information. We use localStorage to remember your timezone and favorite teams. Cloudflare Web Analytics is cookieless."
  pageHeading="Privacy Policy"
>

  <p class="text-xs text-slate-dim">Last updated: 2026-05-21</p>

  <p>
    KickoffWhen is built to respect your privacy. We do not require sign-ups, do not run any cross-site
    trackers, and do not sell or share data with anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, email, phone or address</li>
    <li>Your IP address (beyond what Cloudflare's edge needs to deliver the page)</li>
    <li>Browsing history outside this site</li>
    <li>Anything that could identify you personally</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we store locally on your device</h2>
  <p>
    To remember your preferences across visits we use your browser's <code>localStorage</code>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>kickoffwhen.timezone</code> — the timezone you picked from the dropdown</li>
    <li><code>kickoffwhen.favorites</code> — slugs of teams you tapped the ⭐ on</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Both stay in your browser. They are not sent to our servers. Clearing your browser data resets them.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>,
    which is cookieless and does not fingerprint visitors. It tells us aggregate page-view counts and rough geography
    (country level). No individual session is identifiable.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> use Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, or any third-party tracking SDK.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    KickoffWhen itself sets no cookies. Cloudflare may set a single <code>__cf_bm</code> bot-detection
    cookie purely for security; it expires in 30 minutes and contains no personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Calendar downloads (.ics)</h2>
  <p>
    When you click "Add to calendar" on a team page, your browser downloads a static <code>.ics</code> file.
    Importing it into Google / Apple / Outlook is handled entirely by those apps — we have no visibility.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    We link to Wikipedia, GitHub and stadium-info sites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    KickoffWhen does not knowingly target children under 13. Since we collect no PII at all, no special
    children's-data flows apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially, we'll update the "Last updated" date at the top and announce on the
    homepage. Since we don't have your email, we can't notify you directly — please check back.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: open an issue at
    <a href="https://github.com/yubudong/kickoffwhen/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/yubudong/kickoffwhen/issues</a>.
  </p>

</LegalLayout>
